## A Sobering Statistic to Digest

This year alone, we've witnessed 217 Class I food recalls – the category reserved for situations where there is a reasonable probability that the use of the product will cause serious adverse health consequences or death. These recall numbers underscore the critical importance of food safety as a consumer issue.

## The Hall of Shame

Among the brands with the most egregious safety records this year:

- **Spring & Mulberry Inc.** has racked up 11 recalls, all classified as Class I. This is a company that should be at the forefront of your caution list.
- **Moonlight Packing Corporation** matches Spring & Mulberry's record with the same number of high-risk recalls.

## Recent Offenders

Just this month, we've seen recalls from Adams Extract & Spice LLC, Fresh & Ready Foods LLC, and Trafa Pharmaceutical Inc. The reasons range from undeclared allergens to contamination with Salmonella. The product diversity spans from spice mixes and dessert shells to chicken fillets and marshmallows.

## Monthly Recall Trends

June 2026 saw a substantial spike, with 212 recalls compared to May's 173. As we step into July, the downward trend suggests a slight reprieve, but not enough to relax vigilance.

## Stay Safe, Stay Informed

Consumers, keep in mind: recalls can happen to any product from any brand at any time. Check expiration dates, maintain awareness of products you've purchased, and stay informed through reliable sources.
